## How to Run

1. Compile the project:

```bash
make compile
```

2. Start the server:

```bash
make server
```

3. Open in a browser:

```text
http://localhost:8080/
http://localhost:8080/about
```

4. Simulate multiple clients from different terminals:

```bash
make client CLIENT_NAME=ClientA CLIENT_MESSAGE="Hello from Client A" PAGE=/
make client CLIENT_NAME=ClientB CLIENT_MESSAGE="Hello from Client B" PAGE=/about
```

## Why This Project Is Useful

This project demonstrates the core backend concepts behind real-world servers:

- multiple clients can connect at the same time
- each request may be processed independently
- server logic must handle concurrency safely and efficiently
- HTTP responses are generated from backend code

## Skills Demonstrated

- Java backend development
- Networking and sockets
- Multithreading and concurrency
- HTTP fundamentals
- Simple web server design

## Resume-Friendly Summary

Developed a multithreaded Java web server that accepts multiple client connections, serves static HTML pages, and handles HTTP requests concurrently using Java sockets and threads.
